# Nothing at the repository root is tracked unless it is named here.
#
# The root is where the build drops things: `go build ./cmd/<name>` writes
# a binary called <name> beside these files, and a builder run without -o
# writes <name>.json there too. Listing those by name is what this file
# used to do, and it went wrong the way an enumeration does - cmd/gundam
# and cmd/palworld were added, nobody extended the list, and an 8.7MB
# binary was committed three times before anyone noticed. The history had
# to be rewritten to get it out.
#
# So the default is now no, and the exceptions are the seven things that
# genuinely live here. A new game needs no change to this file; a new root
# file that does belong gets one line, and until it does `git add` says so
# out loud rather than quietly taking a binary.
#
# The negation cannot be written as `cmd/*` or anything like it: that
# would ignore the builders' own source. Only the root is denied, and
# every directory named below is walked normally.
/*

!/.github/
!/cmd/
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/go.mod
!/go.sum
